From ddbbeab4419035c542b69f4211866f54954b496b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Beri <jmberi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:46:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] samples: cpp: synchronization: match thread entry to
 k_thread_entry_t

coop_thread_entry() is declared void f(void) and cast to
k_thread_entry_t, which the kernel calls with three arguments. Calling a
function through an incompatible function type is undefined behaviour,
and it traps on targets that check indirect calls.

Give the entry the signature k_thread_entry_t declares, and drop the cast
that hid the mismatch.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01APoUNc1caCDU2PVRFEQRyi
---
 samples/cpp/cpp_synchronization/src/main.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/samples/cpp/cpp_synchronization/src/main.cpp b/samples/cpp/cpp_synchronization/src/main.cpp
index 3ccf39bbb28..d9dcc82c287 100644
--- a/samples/cpp/cpp_synchronization/src/main.cpp
+++ b/samples/cpp/cpp_synchronization/src/main.cpp
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@ void cpp_semaphore::give(void)
 cpp_semaphore sem_main;
 cpp_semaphore sem_coop;
 
-void coop_thread_entry(void)
+void coop_thread_entry(void *, void *, void *)
 {
 	struct k_timer timer;
 
@@ -135,7 +135,7 @@ int main(void)
 	struct k_timer timer;
 
 	k_thread_create(&coop_thread, coop_stack, STACKSIZE,
-			(k_thread_entry_t) coop_thread_entry,
+			coop_thread_entry,
 			NULL, NULL, NULL, K_PRIO_COOP(7), 0, K_NO_WAIT);
 	k_timer_init(&timer, NULL, NULL);
 
